<title>USA: BPA offers firm power heavy-load power Fri and Sat.</title>
<headline>BPA offers firm power heavy-load power Fri and Sat.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) offered up to 200 megawatts (MW) of firm power during heavy-load hours, 0600-2200 PST, on Friday and Saturday, the federal agency said Thursday.</p>
<p>The offer ends a 6-day streak in which BPA refrained from surplus power sales.</p>
<p>The agency's price for Friday and Saturday is $26.00 per megawatt hour for Northwest deliveries and $27.00 for California-Oregon border (COB) deliveries.</p>
<p>Before it withdrew from offering surplus power late last week, BPA offered firm heavy-load power at $25.50 in the Northwest and $26.50 for COB.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
</text>
